      "key": "descra",
      "label": "Description",
      "searchable": true,
      "value": "Stapled program printed in black ink on white paper. Titled \"\"An evening of Black contemporary films.\"\" the 1975 Brockman Film Festival took place at the Scottish Rites Auditorium on Wilshire Boulevard. The program lists the evening's schedule, as well as brief remarks from organizers and credits to supporters. Filme included Roberta Flack's Legend of John Henry, Charlesetta Turner's Little Black Riding Hood, Stanley Taylor's Bloods Way, John C. Clark's Apres le silence, Madeline Anderson's Malcolm X, Ed McAllister's Karate, Betye Saar's Colored Spade, a segment of Superfly, and more. Michele Maddox gave an introduction and films were interspersed with performances by mime Hayward Coleman. "
    },
